// add world messages starting at 0.  You may use up to 999

{0}{This is a TEMPORARY variable. It is used to store the line number that we want dialog to continue with in the Mayor/PC/Treasurer dialogue exchange. It also stores how much the PC is depositing or withdrawing from their account at the bank. ONLY TEMPORARY Numbers are to be stored here. A number is usually stored here and then accessed in a script straight afterwards. (I use this because I can't set Local Variables in the Dialogue)}
{1}{This is a SECOND TEMPORARY variable. Currently, it is used to store the item the PC requested to buy from the General Store Salesman. The basic prototype of this item will be created in the PC's inventory. It also stores the line that Dialogue will continue with in the Bank Teller Deposit/Withdrawal script.}
{2}{How much hard moola (coins) this PC has in their bank account. IE: The current account balance.}